{"output":"I’ll inspect the search code and test setup, add a minimal stale-request guard, and run the existing tests.\n\nThe controller let every request update state, even after a newer search started. I added a request ID check for results, errors, and loading; clearing the query also invalidates pending requests. The existing tests don’t cover these races, so I’ll check them with an inline script without modifying test files.\n\nFixed src/search/controller.ts so only the latest search can update results, errors, or loading. Clearing the query immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API and normal behavior are unchanged.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests; six inline race scenarios passed; git diff --check passed. Exit code 0. No tests modified or dependencies installed.","final_output":"Fixed src/search/controller.ts so only the latest search can update results, errors, or loading. Clearing the query immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API and normal behavior are unchanged.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests; six inline race scenarios passed; git diff --check passed. Exit code 0. No tests modified or dependencies installed.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":10,"tool_calls":[{"name":"glob_files","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"git status --short","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-jm2sn40h/5-2-optimized/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":191,"stdout_bytes":0,"stderr_bytes":42,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-015f7992ae99e459ef3b2bcb625fc38b.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"npm test && node --input-type=module <<'NODE'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { createSearchController } from './src/search/controller.ts';\nconst items = [{ id: 'new', title: 'New', url: '/new' }];\nfor (const outcome of ['resolve', 'reject']) {\n  for (const timing of ['pending', 'completed', 'cleared']) {\n    const requests = [];\n    const c = createSearchController({ search: () => new Promise((resolve, reject) => requests.push({ resolve, reject })) });\n    const old = c.search('old');\n    const current = c.search('new');\n    if (timing === 'completed') { requests[1].resolve(items); await current; }\n    if (timing === 'cleared') {\n      await c.search('  ');\n      assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: '', results: [], loading: false, error: null });\n    }\n    const before = c.getState();\n    if (outcome === 'resolve') requests[0].resolve([{ ...items[0], id: 'old' }]);\n    else requests[0].reject(new Error('stale failure'));\n    await old;\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), before);\n    if (timing !== 'completed') {\n      requests[1].resolve(items); await current;\n      if (timing === 'cleared') assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), before);\n      else assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: 'new', results: items, loading: false, error: null });\n    }\n  }\n}\nconsole.log('Passed 6 deferred-request race scenarios');\nNODE\n git diff --check && git diff --stat && git diff -- src/search/controller.ts","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-jm2sn40h/5-2-optimized/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":366,"stdout_bytes":2262,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-51bb94529f4452b588fbfe15b2b0fbe6.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}}],"usage":{"input_tokens":28881,"output_tokens":1025},"usage_details":{"cached_input_tokens":8704,"cache_write_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":9}}
